  "question": {
    "text": "A ray of light is incident along a line which meets another line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. The ray is then reflected from this point along the line&nbsp;<math><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. Then the equation of the line of incidence of the ray of light is :"
